In article <1991Feb19.083822.19029@portia.Stanford.EDU> toddc@portia.Stanford.EDU (Todd C. Merrill) writes:
>What does the attribute HD mean? 

Hit Dice, from role playing games.  The HD number is equivalent to a
level for humans.  Each extra HD means it is more likely that a monster
will gain a hit on a particular armour class, and each HD represents a
random number of hit points from 1-8. Thus a Xorn with HD of 8 will have
anywhere from 8-64 hit points (of course, this *is* a bell curve). And
a Master Lich with 17 HD will likely have more hit points and would
stand a MUCH greater chance of registering a hit.

